ETHERNET_PORT CONFIG
These are tips from the ARENA SDK documentation for Linux to achieve best communication possible over ethernet.

CHECK eno1 PARAMS (port closest to power): These should all be set correctly on startup, but feel free to check.

ip link show eno1
	- should show mtu 9000
	- MTU is persistent via NetworkManager (set by install.sh / update.sh)

ethtool -g eno1
	- RX and TX max is 1024 on this hardware; current settings should already be at max by default
	- No manual configuration needed

This config file below is responsible for network memory settings
sudo nano /etc/sysctl.d/99-custom.conf

sysctl net.core.rmem_default
sysctl net.core.rmem_max
	- Confirm you get 33554432
	- Deployed automatically by install.sh / update.sh

